  "boundaries": [
    "Finite caller-anchored repair fetching prerequisite only. No repair CLI, replacement writes, quarantine, resumable publication or automatic startup repair.",
    "Caller must select an intact current consensus anchor, stage every delivered complete block and revalidate selection before publication. Completion proves delivery, not staging or EVM execution.",
    "Descending cursor retains bounded header/page and per-block payload/extraction work. Inputs and lifetime limits are caller selected; network decoding and total RSS are not covered by postdecode work limits.",
    "Failed or dropped polled operation leaves terminal cursor. Absolute deadline includes staging and is observed between synchronous CPU steps. It does not preempt CPU or revoke admitted Reth wire requests.",
    "Maintenance lifecycle must own networking teardown and runtime responsiveness. Existing peer cache may be persisted; no normal storage progress or repair publication is invoked.",
    "Existing validators/extractor and explicit-limit request policies reused. Default live/historical ingestion paths, storage formats, dependencies and toolchain unchanged; no benchmark or throughput claim.",
    "Initial draft compile failed from unsupported future Send promise and Display-only validator error conversion; focused Clippy found a large enum variant. Corrected before source freeze, not original-repository bug claims.",
    "Focused controls use finite disconnected/scripted fixtures and dormant loopback fixture only; no production data, remote host or live sync.",
    "Remaining offline repair coordinator, policy decisions, integrated acceptance and live/staging gates remain open."
  ]
